<title>BELGIUM: EU source says lira must go in below 1,000 v mark.</title>
<headline>EU source says lira must go in below 1,000 v mark.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-11-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>An Austrian representative at European Union talks on the lira's re-entry into the Exchange Rate Mechanism said the Italian currency was expected to join at less than 1,000 lira to the mark.</p>
<p>He said that after earlier bilateral talks EU ministers were now holding multilateral negotiations to break the deadlock over the entry rate.  </p>
<p>&quot;They must find a deal at below 1,000 lira per mark,&quot; the Austrian representative said.</p>
<p>He said 14 out of 15 EU countries represented at a meeting in Brussels on the lira re-entry were supporting such an approach.</p>
<p>He said Austria would be happy with 980-985 lira to the mark. He would not comment on what the Italian position currently was.</p>
<p>Earlier, sources said the Italians wanted the lira to enter at 1,000 to the mark or less.</p>
</text>
